Title: The normalize column has no consumer: drivers hardcode the flag the registry now carries
Created: 2026-08-30
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-08-30T16:20Z Minh Ha-Duong created
2026-08-30T16:21Z claude note found by the roar sweep for the day's defect class (a per-model axis a wrapper silently drops — the shape of both the pooling bug and the 0481 device bug). Ticket 0262's exit criterion reads "The driver applies it and records it in every result file"; the column and its guard landed, the application did not.

--- body ---
## Context

`bench/models.json` carries `normalize`/`normalize_source` per model (ticket
0262), guarded by `bench/check_models.py` — and nothing reads it. Every
driver passes a literal: `normalize: false` in the fidelity and recall
embedders, `normalize: true` in the cost drivers. This is the third instance
of one class: pooling was hardcoded `mean` while four candidates want `cls`
(ticket 0421), the device flag was dropped by the sweep wrapper (ticket
0481), and now normalize is declared but unapplied.

Why nothing measured so far is invalidated: every campaign treated all
candidates uniformly, and the retrieval scoring is cosine, which is
normalization-invariant. The axis starts to bite the first time vectors meet
a dot-product consumer (the design's stored-norm scan), a cross-normalize
comparison, or an upstream path that normalizes where ours did not.

## Actions

1. Make the drivers read `normalize` from the registry per model, the way
   pooling and the input template already travel, and record the applied
   value in every result file (0262's original exit criterion, delivered).
2. Where a driver *deliberately* wants raw geometry (fidelity's
   `normalize: false`), say so in a comment naming this ticket, so the
   literal reads as a choice and not the class recurring.
3. Class guard: extend the check that already refuses hardcoded model ids,
   pooling modes and templates in `bench/` to refuse a bare `normalize:`
   literal outside declared exceptions — a registry axis with no consumer is
   this class's larval form.

## Test

- Red first: the class guard must fail against today's tree before the
  drivers are fixed.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Drivers apply the registry's normalize per model and record it
- [ ] Deliberate raw-geometry literals carry the naming comment
- [ ] The guard goes red on a hardcoded normalize and green after the fix
